  "findings": [
    "Inside the training envelope (lambda<=1) all three arms are at or near ceiling; the capability AUC saturates at 1.000 for both DR arms, so that grid has no resolution here.",
    "All separation is OUTSIDE the envelope: at lambda=1.5 success is off 0.564 vs fixed 0.924 and lucid_rg 0.932; at 40 ms latency it is off 0.527 vs 1.000 for both DR arms.",
    "lucid_rg and fixed are indistinguishable on every cell (C_AUC 1.000 vs 1.000, CVaR20 0.998 vs 0.998), which is exactly what H1a predicts when the controller saturates in 57 iterations.",
    "Progress saturates (>=0.86 everywhere) and is a poor discriminator on this task; success rate separates the arms far better at the hard end."
  ],
  "not_yet_verified": [
    "anything across seeds: this is one training seed",
    "lucid_s4_rg, whose intensity mixture is the only LUCID mechanism that survives lambda saturation",
    "that the differences between fixed and lucid_rg (0.008 at lambda=1.5) exceed seed noise; they almost certainly do not"
